# `--code-location ..` makes the whole repo root the build context, and CodeBuild uploads
# that context to S3. Without this file .env (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID / AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY)
# leaves the machine and can land in an image layer. The project rule is that .env is never
# committed and never printed; a build context is the same bar.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.git
.gitignore
_data
_runs
archive
evals
submission
web
benefitlineruntime
deploy
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
*.log
